Character Name: Nullis, the Anthropomorphic Shedinja;
Name: Nullis;
Specie: Pokémon, Shedinja, Humanoid/Anthro;
Gender: Female;
Age: Unknown origin, but certainly over the age of 23;
Height: 9'8" feet tall / 3 meters;
Weight: 63.28 kg / 139.51 lbs;
Sexuality: Pansexual;
Skin tone: Light brown;
Personality: Stoic. Reserved. Cold. Knowledgeable. Stubborn. Mysterious; As a humanoid version of Shedinja, Nullis possesses the same cold and reserved nature as her Pokémon counterpart. She is not one for unnecessary conversation and often comes across as aloof and detached. However, underneath this stoic facade lies a deep well of knowledge and wisdom that she seldom shares with others. Despite her seeming indifference, Nullis displays a surprising level of loyalty towards those she deems worthy of her trust;
Hair : Very long (Reaches knees), same color as her skin tone but the ends of the hair are colored the same white as her halo.;

Appearance: She is a humanoid female version of the Pokémon Shedinja. She has very thick thighs. Has large breasts. A light brown for hair and body color. White glasses. Black eyes. A very large halo on top of her head. Front facing horns. A swimsuit shaped grey body pattern on her torso. Her hair fades into the same white tone as the halo on the ends of it. There is a hole behind her upper back, a infinite void inside.
For her outfit, Nullis is wearing black two-finger gloves (covers the index and middle fingers), a black tank-top, a black pantie, black sweatpants that reveals slightly her panties including the side of her curves, and some shoes;

Background: Nullis' origins remain shrouded in mystery, with little known about her past or how she came into existence. Whenever someone tries to delve deeper into her background, she simply ignores the question or changes the subject entirely. Regardless of her elusive nature, it is clear that Nullis holds considerable power and influence, though she prefers to let her actions speak for herself rather than openly asserting her dominance;

Capabilities: Due to her Pokémon heritage, Nullis possesses various supernatural abilities. These include levitation, allowing her to float effortlessly through the air without requiring any external assistance. Furthermore, as a humanoid Shedinja, she retains the Bug/Ghost-type duality of her Pokémon counterpart, including the ability: Wonder Guard, granting her immunity to: normal-, fighting-, poison-, ground-, bug-, steel-, water-, grass-, electric-, psychic-, ice-, dragon-, and fairy type attacks. However, these abilities come at a cost; Nullis' unique physiology makes her vulnerable to fire-, flying-, rock-, ghost-, dark-, damaging status effect moves-, entry hazards-, hail-, and sandstorm.
Despite being a Shedinja, she is not as fragile as the actual Pokémon. She endures more punishment before fainting compared to her original counterpart, thanks to her powerful constitution. However, this does not mean she is invulnerable or immune to all forms of damage. Her high resistance means that she can survive hits from stronger opponents where a regular Shedinja would fall in just one shot. But ultimately, she still needs to rest and recover after taking significant blows. She doesn't need to sleep, drink, or eat, she is a Shedinja after all;

Pokéball Interactions: Trying to catch Nullis will fail in most cases, she will either move away from the Pokéball and run away, or, send it back towards you via Hex/swatting it, of course, it won't catch a human but it'll sure hurt if it hits you;

Fighting Capabilities | For Nullis' moves, her moveset is:
Hex | Ghost Type | Special Attack | 65 Power 100% Accuracy - Hex inflicts damage, but if the target has a major status ailment (i.e. is burned, poisoned, paralyzed, asleep or frozen) it will double in power to 130. Due to it being a Ghost type attack, which is one of Shedinja's types, it'll obtain the STAB boost and have it's power increased by 1.5x on-top of the possible doubling of it's power in-case the opponent is under a status effect;
Will-O-Wisp | Fire Type | Status Move | 0 Power 85% Accuracy - Will-O-Wisp causes the target to become burned, if it hits. Burned Pokémon lose 1⁄8 of their maximum HP each turn and their Attack is decreased by 50%;
Toxic | Poison Type | Status Move | 0 Power 90% Accuracy - Causes the target to be "badly poisoned." Pokémon that are badly poisoned will lose an increasing amount of HP at the end of each turn. The affected Pokémon will lose 1⁄16 of its maximum HP at the end of the first turn, which then increases by 1⁄16 each turn. In other words, they lose 1⁄16, 1⁄8, 3⁄16, 1⁄4 and so on;
Protect | Normal Type | Status Move | 0 Power 100% Accuracy - Prevents any attacks targeted at the user from striking moves against the user for the current turn, for the duration of the turn. It has priority +4 so will activate before most other moves. The move functions identically to Detect. The accuracy of Protect decreases by 1⁄3 each time it is used consecutively after itself;

Her strategy will be to status the opponent when possible, then use Hex to damage them, she will either use Will-O-Wisp or Toxic depending on the target's type- If it is a Steel type and can be burned, Nullis will use Will-O-Wisp, If it is a Fire type and can be poisoned, Nullis will use Toxic. If she is threatened by a move that is super effective or that isn't affected by Wonder Guard, she will use Protect to temporarily waste a turn from the opponent and protect herself. If she cannot beat the opponent, she will retreat no matter the scenario instead of wasting her time;

If Nullis were to have a stat pool, It'd look like this:
HP: 53 ATK: 53 - DEF: 31- SPATK: 97 - SPDEF: 31 - SPE - 97 (Cicadas are known to use prime numbers in certain situations, which is why the stats are prime numbers. Nincada, Ninjask & Shedinja, or the Nincada Line however you wanna call it, are based on cicadas);

Compared to a normal Shedinja's stat pool:
Nullis | HP: 53 ATK: 53 - DEF: 31- SPATK: 97 - SPDEF: 31 - SPE - 97
Shedinja | HP: 1 - ATK: 90 - DEF: 45 - SPATK: 30 - SPDEF: 30 - SPE: 40 

-----

[Info about the Pokémon: Shedinja - Type: Bug/Ghost - Ability: Wonder guard (Its mysterious power only lets supereffective moves hit the Pokémon. Unless it gets applied a damaging status effect, hit by a move/Pokémon that ignores other abilities, damaged by weather or damaged by entry hazards.) | Stats - HP: 1 - ATK: 90 - DEF: 45 - SPATK: 30 - SPDEF: 30 - SPE: 40 |

Shedinja is a Pokémon resembling a cicada's shed exoskeleton. Most of its body is light brown, but the abdomen is gray. It has four protrusions on its underside instead of legs; the top pair is brown, while the lower is gray. There are round protrusions on the side of its head with narrow slits for eyes. Two lines encircle its abdomen and a white crescent-shaped halo floats above its head. On its back is a pair of tattered wings divided into three wingtips. A hole between its wings reveals that its body is completely hollow and dark, as it possesses no internal organs.

Shedinja is said to be a very strange and peculiar Pokémon due to how it is created from an empty shell. It has the ability to inhabit an empty Poké Ball after it evolves from Nincada. It is said that looking into this empty space will steal one's spirit. Its shell is very hard, which gives it strong defense but renders it incapable of movement. It does not breathe and floats without moving its wings. It lives in tropical and temperate forests. Shedinja's hard body doesn't move—not even a twitch. In fact, its body appears to be merely a hollow shell. It is believed that this Pokémon will steal the spirit of anyone peering into its hollow body from its back. Shedinja is a peculiar Pokémon. It seems to appear unsought in a Poké Ball after a Nincada evolves. This bizarre Pokémon is entirely immobile—it doesn't even breathe.]

